  "problem": "Recipes could not prove exactly what a small request checked. HTTP 200 HTML, missing Census keys, wrong MIME, unexpected fields, empty-but-valid data, ignored row limits, and public examples could be conflated with full dataset/schema validation or leak credentials.",
  "resulting_behavior": "createExampleReceipt stores source/release/distribution, sanitized parameters, expected content/fields, size and row limits, observation time and attempted checks. CMS/CDC sample receipts and Census keyless HTML produce distinct outcomes. executeBoundedSample compares actual fields/types to the receipt independently of catalog classification, and stops on wrong MIME, missing key, unexpected field, empty-but-valid data and ignored row limit. HTTP 200 alone never produces a tested-example badge. Sample field/type checks remain separate from full dataset/schema checks. publishExamplePreview distinguishes sampled values from synthetic schema examples. generateCopyableExamples round-trips limits, context pins and credential placeholders without placing secrets in public artifacts. Live fetch is forbidden. CLI stays fixture-only. Sealed packages/normalization/src and packages/identity/src/schema-catalog.mjs are unchanged.",
